# Testing and verification

Detail: [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) section "Testing and reporting", including "ChatGPT handoff".

A compile is not completion. Say which level ran: unit, integration, regression, packaged GUI, real-world acceptance, or release.

- Drive a changed desktop control. A single screenshot is not a behavior check.
- Do not claim `cargo test` was run unless it was run in this session.
- SMB1, live OpenAI, and Bazzite stay BLOCKED or NOT TESTED until those inputs exist. Do not mark them PASS from a synthetic fixture or a mock.
- Report each gate as PASS, FAIL, BLOCKED, NOT TESTED, or NOT APPLICABLE.
- IMPLEMENTED, TESTED, VERIFIED, and ACCEPTED are different. A typed URL is not an analysis. Raw tiles are not an assembled character. An empty reopened project is not a saved cartridge session.

End every substantial session with one fenced Markdown block titled `NESTICLES — [PHASE / TASK] — STATUS FOR CHATGPT`. That block is the handoff the owner pastes into ChatGPT. Use the twelve headings in AGENTS.md. Keep product failures visible. JSON may be saved as a separate validated file and never replaces this block. Do not print a key or ROM bytes.
